	(text "MCU: ESP32-C3 Rust board (A1) in two socket headers, the same module as the box (D-66). DevKit-RUST-1 Rev 1.2a fitted, RUST-2 also fits.\nPads as the esp-rs Rust_Board footprint: left 1..16, right 28..17 top to bottom (D-93). SDA SEL JP61: 2-3 RUST-1 (SDA IO10), 2-1 RUST-2 (SDA IO7) (D-94). Net labels at the DevKit pins; everything else is wired. 3V3 pin from the LD1117 (power sheet); EN low keeps the board buck off;\n5V not connected. USB-C to the Mac (Delock 64226) or the Pi (D-68).\nDirect GPIO (D-83): IO0 PERMIT_R1, IO1 WDI (kick at least every 0.9 s), IO3 LATCH_CLR (rising edge), IO4 PERMIT_R2, IO5 PERMIT_R3,\nIO6 DATA_TX, IO20 DATA_RX, IO21 SAFE_LOST (boot-ROM log pin, 1k series). SDA IO10 or IO7, SCL IO8 (board 10k pull-ups, SHTC3 0x70, IMU 0x68).\nIO2 (WS2812, strapping) and IO9 (BOOT, strapping) not used. Board LED on IO7 (RUST-1) or IO10 (RUST-2): the SDA pin of the other board.\nFault latch (D-59): FAULT set at power-up, brown-out and watchdog time-out; cleared by a LATCH_CLR edge only when RESET_N is high.\nFAULT goes to the SAFE sheet and blocks every permit in hardware. RESET_N also resets the PCA9539: keys off, SW_STOP_N released.\nPCA9539 0x74 (D-92): IO0_0 SW_STOP_N (out), IO0_1 R1_TX, IO0_2 KEY_R1 (out), IO0_3 BAND_D, IO0_4 BAND_A, IO0_5 BAND_B, IO0_6 BAND_C,\nIO0_7 LED_R1 (out), IO1_0 KEY_R2 (out), IO1_1 R2_TX, IO1_2 LED_R2 (out), IO1_3 KEY_R3 (out), IO1_4 R3_TX, IO1_5 LED_R3 (out),\nIO1_6 KILL_S, IO1_7 LATCHED. Inputs not marked. Write outputs 0 before configuring (F1)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
